{"series":"Epoch Capabilities Index (ECI), every model Epoch scores, by release date","unit":"ECI points: linear, unbounded, rescaled so Claude 3.5 Sonnet = 130 and GPT-5 = 150","description":"Main series: Epoch's composite capability score for all 270 dated models, with Epoch's 90% bootstrap interval (ci90_low, ci90_high; none for the two anchor models), organization and open/closed-weights group. `other_series` holds training compute of notable models, the lowest inference price at fixed scores, and one series per kept benchmark (percent, 0 to 100), each with dated points sorted by date and a `frontier` flag (a new record by date). Bounded benchmark series also carry `crossings`: the dates the frontier crossed 10%, 50% and 90% of the ceiling. Built by experiments/epoch/build.py; see experiments/epoch/README.md.","method":"Item response theory: performance(model m, benchmark b) = sigmoid(alpha_b * (C_m - D_b)). Capabilities C_m, difficulties D_b and slopes alpha_b are fit jointly to every score by non-linear least squares with a ridge penalty, with no time or compute term. Scores enter normalized by each benchmark's random baseline and max-achievable ceiling, as the best score per model group. Models need at least 4 benchmarks. 90% intervals come from 500 bootstrap refits. Source: https://epoch.ai/data/eci-documentation/methodology and https://github.com/epoch-research/eci-public; paper: https://www.arxiv.org/abs/2512.00193.","interpretation":"The scale is arbitrary but linear: Epoch means +10 from 100 to 110 to be as impressive as from 140 to 150. There is no maximum. At launch, Epoch found about +5 ECI matched a doubling of METR's time horizon. Absolute slopes mean nothing; changes in slope do. The joint fit is rerun as data arrives, so old models' values can shift slightly between downloads, and the calibration points may be revisited.","license":"CC BY 4.0. Credit: Epoch AI, 'Capabilities & benchmarking', 'Epoch Capabilities Index' and 'Data on AI models', and Cottier, Snodin, Owen and Adamczewski, 'LLM inference prices have fallen rapidly but unequally across tasks' (Epoch AI data insight, Mar 12, 2025); epoch.ai, accessed 2026-10-21. Epoch's download notes that results it copies from external projects keep their original licensing: see each series' `runs`.","retrieved":"2026-10-21","sources":["https://epoch.ai/data/benchmark_data.zip (linked from https://epoch.ai/benchmarks/use-this-data; retrieved 2026-10-21T07:33:36Z; 2,356,346 bytes; sha256 d028f2aa787630655329063db9b535aae48641cb5626b27e7bf7aad61aaffd40)","https://epoch.ai/data/notable_ai_models.csv (linked from https://epoch.ai/data/ai-models; retrieved 2026-10-21T07:33:37Z; 2,261,918 bytes; sha256 3ef26619430a93ee4d126bc46e91699fe6f2b15ea7b8e830f0a565e32caaa224)","https://epoch.ai/data/charts/llm-inference-price-trends/lowest_price_models_data.csv (linked from https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends; retrieved 2026-10-21T07:33:38Z; 11,563 bytes; sha256 cb4f44d88b39e147b23ac5ff632c8a7a443729487c13c7b76f1c92987708fbc4)","https://epoch.ai/data/charts/llm-inference-price-trends/other_models_data.csv (linked from https://epoch.ai/data-insights/llm-inference-price-trends; retrieved 2026-10-21T07:33:38Z; 26,624 bytes; sha256 58a02792788ee513e1a3f43df51ddd308f4826ac47377767a59ac52d9f05e2ce)","https://epoch.ai/eci and https://epoch.ai/data/eci-documentation/methodology (ECI definition)","https://github.com/epoch-research/eci-public at e937446cd8ac0e910ea578516b1cab2b00c06d25, src/eci/dataloader.py (meaning of score_ceiling, model_group, max per group)","https://epoch.ai/benchmarks/<slug> for each series' level wording and human baselines; https://epoch.ai/benchmarks/search for review verdicts and domains (all read 2026-10-21)"],"caveats":["Dates are model release dates, not evaluation dates: Epoch ran many models long after release, so a frontier by release date is drawn in hindsight.","External series mix harnesses and reporters; developer-reported scores (MMLU, GSM8K and the other 2019-2024 sets) are often best-of settings chosen by the lab.","Each point is the best score among a model group's settings on that date (reasoning effort, scaffold, provider), as Epoch's ECI does; the low-effort variants are not separate points.","Frontier means a strictly higher score than every earlier point; ties do not count, and same-day releases yield at most one frontier point.","Each crossing rung is one of: {date} (interpolated linearly between the straddling frontier points, so it usually falls between releases), {date: F, upper_bound: true} (already above at the first dated point F, so F is only an upper bound) or {date: null, open_as_of: L} (not crossed in data ending at L); date is null only when the rung was not crossed. Several sets stopped being updated in 2024 or 2025, so an open rung marks where the data ends, not a plateau. Multiple-choice sets put the 10% rung (and two-choice sets the 50% rung) at or below chance.","Rows with a score but no release date are dropped (counts.undated_rows), as on Epoch's charts. Where some of them beat the dated record, the series says so in `undated_above_record`; there the record and the rungs are lower or later than the full table suggests.","human_baseline.first_at_or_above is the first model at or above the human figure, with its actual release date; human_baseline.interpolated is the ladder-style interpolated date, which no model actually matched.","Superseded series are kept for history; do not join them to their successors. FrontierMath v2 fixed errors in 42% of problems; ProofBench was re-graded on 2026-08-14 with corrected formalizations and a stricter grader, and Epoch marks the v1.0-era rows not comparable, so the file splits ProofBench by grading.","A point with a `note` flags a likely error in Epoch's data, kept as published (Video-MME: VideoLLaMA 3 dated a year before its paper).","In developer-reported series an early report can stand as the record for years; these series have a single frontier point: boolq, lambada. BoolQ's is T5-11B's 91.2 from the T5 paper (Oct 2019) and LAMBADA's MT-NLG 530B (Oct 2021); neither is beaten in Epoch's table, so those frontiers say more about who reported what than about capability.","Benchmark points are dated by the version that scored them, as its CSV gives it; Gemini 2.5 Pro's GA version keeps 2025-06-17, though Epoch dates its group 2025-06-05.","ECI points use Epoch's group dates. For 15 of the 17 ECI models whose versions shipped on different dates, that is the latest version's date (GPT-4 Turbo (Nov 2023) is dated 2024-01-25, though gpt-4-1106-preview shipped 2023-11-06). That matches the index, which takes each group's best score across versions: the earliest date would credit later versions' scores to it.","Epoch's reviews rate HLE, SWE-bench Verified and DeepSWE flawed (see `epoch_review`).","The ECI is refit jointly, so its values move a little with every download; pin to this file's retrieval date when citing."],"points":[{"date":"2023-02-24","value":109.97,"model":"LLaMA-65B","frontier":true,"ci90_low":100.74,"ci90_high":114.32,"org":"Meta AI","access":"Open weights"},{"date":"2023-02-24","value":107.18,"model":"LLaMA-33B","frontier":false,"ci90_low":97.05,"ci90_high":111.91,"org":"Meta AI","access":"Open weights"},{"date":"2023-02-24","value":100.32,"model":"LLaMA-13B","frontier":false,"ci90_low":89.05,"ci90_high":106.42,"org":"Meta AI","access":"Open weights"},{"date":"2023-02-24","value":96.62,"model":"LLaMA-7B","frontier":false,"ci90_low":83.72,"ci90_high":103.51,"org":"Meta AI","access":"Open weights"},{"date":"2023-03-14","value":125.74,"model":"GPT-4 (Mar 2023)","frontier":true,"ci90_low":120.54,"ci90_high":131.03,"org":"OpenAI","access":"Closed weights"},{"date":"2023-03-20","value":82.66,"model":"Cerebras-GPT-13B","frontier":false,"ci90_low":66.35,"ci90_high":91.36,"org":"Cerebras Systems","access":"Open weights"},{"date":"2023-04-11","value":89.2,"model":"Dolly 2.0-12b","fro